save_tcod_total_energy
_name.category_id                CATEGORY_OVERVIEW
_definition.update               2026-10-26
_definition.class                Set
_definition.scope                Category
_definition.id                   TCOD_TOTAL_ENERGY
_name.object_id                  TCOD_TOTAL_ENERGY
save_
save_tcod_total_energy_value
_name.category_id                tcod_total_energy
_units.code                      electron_volts
_description.text
; Ideally, should correspond to
https://www.xml-cml.org/dictionary/compchem/ "total energy" (ID:
totalEnergy) whenever applicable.

The total energy for a system of electrons and nuclei. The exact
method of computing this parameter depends on the method. The formula
used to compute it should be given in the _tcod_total_energy_formula
data item; in CIF2 this will be a DRel method (i.e. a formal
computable expression in a strictly specified computer language).

CAUTION: total energies are comparable only between computations made
by the same method, under the same approximations and with the same or
similar input parameters. Therefore, the value of this data item
*SHOULD NOT* be used to rank different TCOD entries without proper
scaling, analysis and justification.
;
_definition.update               2026-10-26
_definition.class                Datum
_type.container                  Single
_type.contents                   Real
_definition.id                   '_tcod_total_energy_value'
_name.object_id                  '_tcod_total_energy_value'
